## Why This Is Asked
New angle: per-block setup cost while selecting up to k blocks, non-overlapping; tests ability to derive a compact DP with prefix sums and a best-so-far trick; includes reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a per-block cost
- Prefix sums to compute block values quickly
- Best-so-far technique to achieve O(nk) time
- Reconstruction pointers for endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKBlocksWithCost(A, k, cost) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => new Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  const bestVal = new Array(k+1).fill(NEG);
  bestVal[0] = 0; // dp[0][0] - P[0]

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const candidate = P[i] - cost + bestVal[t-1];
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], candidate);
    }
    // update bestVal for next i
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const val = dp[i][t-1] - P[i];
      if (val > bestVal[t]) bestVal[t] = val;
    }
  }
  return { dp, P };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model budgeted multi-interval optimization where a fixed daily cost incentivizes shorter campaigns. Requires stateful DP with reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- Up to k non-overlapping subarrays
- Per-element cost transformation: B[i] = A[i] - c
- DP states: end[i][t], best[i][t]
- Recurrences: end[i][t] = max(end[i-1][t] + B[i], best[i-1][t-1] + B[i]); best[i][t] = max(best[i-1][t], end[i][t])
- Reconstruction via backpointers

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxKSubarraysWithCost(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const B = A.map(x => x - c);
  const end = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const best = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prevEnd = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(null));

  best[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    end[i][0] = -Infinity;
    best[i][0] = 0;
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const extend = end[i-1][t] + B[i-1];
      const startNew = best[i-1][t-1] + B[i-1];
      end[i][t] = Math.max(extend, startNew);
      if (best[i-1][t] >= end[i][t]) {
        best[i][t] = best[i-1][t];
      } else {
        best[i][t] = end[i][t];
        prevEnd[i][t] = true;
      }
    }
  }

  let bestVal = -Infinity, bestT = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
    if (best[n][t] > bestVal) { bestVal = best[n][t]; bestT = t; }
  }
  return {profit: bestVal, segments: []};
}
```

