## Why This Problem Is Asked
This problem combines prefix DP with an inner backward sweep to compute the optimal segment ending at each position. It tests understanding of state decomposition, reconstruction logic, and handles edge cases like negative values naturally.

## Key Concepts
- DP state: dp[i][t] tracks the optimal value using the first i elements with t segments
- Inner loop: expanding the left boundary computes segment maximum on the fly
- Reconstruction: store predecessor pointers to recover exact subarray boundaries
- Complexity: O(n²k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueSubarrays(A, k) {
    const n = A.length;
    const dp = Array(n + 1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
    const prev = Array(n + 1).fill(null).map(() => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
    dp[0][0] = 0;

    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
            let curMax = -Infinity;
            for (let l = i; l >= 1; l--) {
                curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[l - 1]);
                const val = (dp[l - 1][t - 1] !== -Infinity ? dp[l - 1][t - 1] + curMax : -Infinity);
                if (val > dp[i][t]) {
                    dp[i][t] = val;
                    prev[i][t] = l;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    const result = [];
    let i = n, t = k;
    while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
        const l = prev[i][t];
        result.unshift([l, i]);
        i = l - 1;
        t--;
    }
    return { value: dp[n][k], boundaries: result };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with a non-adjacent selection constraint and exact count, forcing clarity on state definition and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP on two dimensions (i, t) with take/skip choices. 
- Non-adjacency enforced by using i-2 when taking i. 
- Backtracking recovers chosen indices; space optimization possible.

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKNonAdjacent(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(false));
  for(let i=0;i<=n;i++) dp[i][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      const val = (i>=2 ? dp[i-2][t-1] : (t===1 ? 0 : -Infinity)) + A[i-1];
      if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = true; }
    }
  }
  let res = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(i>0 && t>0){
    if(take[i][t]){ res.push(i); i-=2; t--; } else { i--; }
  }
  res.reverse();
  return {sum: dp[n][k], indices: res};
}
```

